msgstr ""

#: appPlugins/ToolIsolation/IsolationUI.py:691
msgid "Also add one path along the boundary outline."
msgstr ""

#: appPlugins/ToolIsolation/IsolationUI.py:721
msgid ""
"Sampling step along the copper boundaries for the Voronoi strategy,\n"
"in the application units (mm or inch). This bounds sample intervals, not "
"the toolpath error.\n"
"The run stops with a message when the 20000 sample-site budget is "
"exceeded;\n"
"increase the spacing instead of lowering the requested accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: appPlugins/ToolIsolation/IsolationUI.py:735
msgid ""
"After Voronoi generation, add partial cuts around flashed pad outlines with "
"the same cutter and depth.\n"
"Original trace and polygon connections stay intact; pads inside pours may "
"have no safe room.\n"
"Region-only and negative images are skipped. This is not solder mask or "
"guaranteed thermal relief.\n"
"The combined paths use normal CNC path ordering, not a separate machining "
"phase."
msgstr ""

#: appPlugins/ToolIsolation/IsolationUI.py:756
msgid ""
"Create a Geometry object with toolpaths to cut \n"
"isolation outside, inside or on both sides of the\n"
"object. For a Gerber object outside means outside\n"
"of the Gerber feature and inside means inside of\n"
"the Gerber feature, if possible at all. This means\n"
"that only if the Gerber feature has openings inside, they\n"
"will be isolated. If what is wanted is to cut isolation\n"
"inside the actual Gerber feature, use a negative tool\n"
"diameter above."
msgstr ""

